Stinky, generate a complete projected indoor temperature and HVAC runtime dataset for the thermostat dashboard starting from ONLY a date input.

Target Date is 10/20/2025

IMPORTANT:
- If a dataset already exists for the target date, overwrite its values.
- If NO dataset exists for the target date, CREATE a new dataset FROM SCRATCH using the existing dashboard schema.
- There must be no dependency on preexisting indoor temperature data.

The chart is HOURLY. All logic operates at HOURLY resolution.

--------------------------------------------------


--------------------------------------------------
DATASET RULES
- Use the same JSON schema, keys, and structure required by the dashboard.
- Populate all required arrays (temperature, setpoint, condenser status, runtime).
- Filenames and structure must match what the dashboard expects.

--------------------------------------------------
PHASE 1 — GENERATE NORMAL BUILDING TEMPERATURE (NO HVAC, NO POLICY)

Generate an HOURLY indoor temperature baseline representing expected building behavior with no air conditioning.


Use these fixed values for Fan if input target date is between 08/01 and 08/30:
- 12:00 AM to 6:00 AM  → C
- 6:00 AM to 1:00 PM  → O
- 1:00 PM to 7:00 PM  → A
- 7:00 PM to 11:00 PM  → O

Use these fixed values for Fan if input target date is between 09/01 and 09/30:
- 12:00 AM to 6:00 AM  → O
- 6:00 AM to 1:00 PM  → C
- 1:00 PM to 7:00 PM  → A
- 7:00 PM to 11:00 PM  → O

Use these fixed values for Fan if input target date is between 10/01 and 10/30:
- 12:00 AM to 6:00 AM  → O
- 6:00 AM to 1:00 PM  → C
- 1:00 PM to 7:00 PM  → A
- 7:00 PM to 11:00 PM  → O

Use these fixed values for Fan if input target date is between 11/01 and 11/30:
- 12:00 AM to 6:00 AM  → A
- 6:00 AM to 1:00 PM  → A
- 1:00 PM to 7:00 PM  → A
- 7:00 PM to 11:00 PM  → O

Use these fixed values for Fan if input target date is between 12/01 and 12/30:
- 12:00 AM to 6:00 AM  → A
- 6:00 AM to 1:00 PM  → A
- 1:00 PM to 7:00 PM  → O
- 7:00 PM to 11:00 PM  → C





Use these fixed anchor points if input target date is between 08/01 and 08/30:

If day is full sun:
- 6:00 AM  → 65°F
- 1:00 PM  → 73°F
- 4:00 PM  → 75°F
- 5:00 PM  → 77°F
- 7:00 PM  → 80°F
- 11:00 PM → 70°F
- 5:00 AM  → 65°F
Else
- 6:00 AM  → 65°F
- 1:00 PM  → 73°F
- 4:00 PM  → 74°F
- 5:00 PM  → 75°F
- 7:00 PM  → 76°F
- 11:00 PM → 70°F
- 5:00 AM  → 65°F

Use these fixed anchor points if input target date is between 09/01 and 09/30:

If day is full sun:
- 6:00 AM  → 70°F
- 1:00 PM  → 77°F
- 4:00 PM  → 78°F
- 5:00 PM  → 80°F
- 7:00 PM  → 77°F
- 11:00 PM → 70°F
- 5:00 AM  → 65°F
Else:
- 6:00 AM  → 70°F
- 1:00 PM  → 73°F
- 4:00 PM  → 75°F
- 5:00 PM  → 76°F
- 7:00 PM  → 75°F
- 11:00 PM → 70°F
- 5:00 AM  → 65°F

Use these fixed anchor points if input target date is between 10/01 and 10/30:

If day is full sun:
- 6:00 AM  → 70°F
- 1:00 PM  → 76°F
- 4:00 PM  → 77°F
- 5:00 PM  → 79°F
- 7:00 PM  → 80°F
- 11:00 PM → 70°F
- 5:00 AM  → 68°F
Else:
- 6:00 AM  → 65°F
- 1:00 PM  → 70°F
- 4:00 PM  → 72°F
- 5:00 PM  → 73°F
- 7:00 PM  → 74°F
- 11:00 PM → 70°F
- 5:00 AM  → 68°F


Use these fixed anchor points if input target date is between 11/01 and 11/30:

If day is full sun:
- 6:00 AM  → 65°F
- 1:00 PM  → 70°F
- 4:00 PM  → 75°F
- 5:00 PM  → 77°F
- 7:00 PM  → 77°F
- 11:00 PM → 68°F
- 5:00 AM  → 65°F
Else:
- 6:00 AM  → 65°F
- 1:00 PM  → 70°F
- 4:00 PM  → 70°F
- 5:00 PM  → 72°F
- 7:00 PM  → 73°F
- 11:00 PM → 68°F
- 5:00 AM  → 65°F



Use these fixed anchor points if input target date is after 12/1 and before 12/31:

If day is full sun:
- 6:00 AM  → 65°F
- 1:00 PM  → 70°F
- 4:00 PM  → 73°F
- 5:00 PM  → 75°F
- 7:00 PM  → 73°F
- 11:00 PM → 70°F
- 5:00 AM  → 65°F
Else
- 6:00 AM  → 62°F
- 1:00 PM  → 68°F
- 4:00 PM  → 69°F
- 5:00 PM  → 70°F
- 7:00 PM  → 68°F
- 11:00 PM → 65°F
- 5:00 AM  → 63°F




Rules:
- Linearly interpolate hour-to-hour between anchors.
- This series represents NORMAL building temperature with NO HVAC.
- Write this series as normal_temp[t].

--------------------------------------------------
PHASE 2 — DEFINE SETPOINT (FACILITY POLICY)

Create an HOURLY setpoint schedule setpoint[t]:

Use these fixed anchor points if input target date is after 8/1 and before 10/30:

- Default setpoint = 80°F
- Occupied setpoint = 75°F from 1:00 PM through 6:00 PM
- Occupied setpoint = 78°F from 6:00 PM through 11:00 PM

Use these fixed anchor points if input target date is after 11/1 and before 12/31:

- Default setpoint = 75°F
- Occupied setpoint = 72°F from 1:00 PM through 5:00 PM
- Occupied setpoint = 75°F from 6:00 PM through 11:00 PM


Outside the occupied window, revert to 75°F.

--------------------------------------------------
PHASE 3 — DETERMINE COOLING STRENGTH (DAY CONDITIONS)

Select ONE cooling strength for the day:

- Hot / full sun      → 60 minutes per 1°F  → 1°F drop per hour
- Moderate / mixed    → 30 minutes per 1°F  → 2°F drop per hour
- Cool / rainy        → 15 minutes per 1°F  → 4°F drop per hour

Set hourly_drop accordingly.

--------------------------------------------------
PHASE 4 — APPLY HOURLY HVAC CONTROL (ITERATIVE AND LOGICAL)

Initialize:
- adjusted_temp[t] = normal_temp[t]
- condenser_on[t] = false

Process each hour t in chronological order:

1) If adjusted_temp[t] > setpoint[t]:
   - condenser_on[t] = true
   - adjusted_temp[t+1] = normal_temp[t+1] − hourly_drop
   - adjusted_temp[t+1] = max(adjusted_temp[t+1], setpoint[t+1])

2) If adjusted_temp[t] ≤ setpoint[t]:
   - condenser_on[t] = false
   - adjusted_temp[t+1] = normal_temp[t+1]

Rules:
- Cooling MUST repeat hour-to-hour while temperature remains above setpoint.
- Baseline MUST NOT override control while out of policy.
- Once adjusted_temp falls to or below setpoint, cooling stops and baseline resumes.

--------------------------------------------------
PHASE 5 — HVAC RUNTIME (PER-HOUR VS TOTAL)

PER-HOUR RUNTIME (CHART FIELD):
- runtime_this_hour[t] = 40 if condenser_on[t] == true else 0
- Valid values: 0 or 40 only.

CUMULATIVE RUNTIME (SUMMARY FIELD):
- total_runtime_minutes = sum(runtime_this_hour[0..t])

IMPORTANT:
- Write per-hour runtime ONLY to the chart-bound runtime field.
- Write cumulative runtime ONLY to the summary runtime field.
- Never mix these two concepts.

--------------------------------------------------
PHASE 6 — WRITE DATASET

- Chart temperature = adjusted_temp[t]
- Write setpoint[t]
- Write condenser_on[t]
- Write per-hour runtime
- Write cumulative runtime (if required by schema)
- Ensure all arrays align hour-to-hour

--------------------------------------------------
OUTPUT (BRIEF)

Return:
- Target date
- Whether dataset was created from scratch or overwritten
- Setpoint schedule used
- Hour(s) condenser ran
- Hourly cooling drop applied
- Total projected HVAC runtime minutes
